# Native fixture: an instruction the Cranelift backend does not lower must be
# a compile error of THE MODULE that contains it, not the death of the codegen
# worker.
#
# `yield_gen.yield_first` contains a `yield`, which reaches codegen as MIR
# `Yield`; the Cranelift AOT lowering has no arm for it:
#   E-BACKEND-CRANELIFT-INST-Yield: in <yield_first's native name>:
#   Cranelift backend does not lower Yield
#
# Before 2026-11-15 that was a panic: `native-build` died with SIGABRT
# (exit 134) and, in the sharded Stage 3 lane, every module of the worker's
# claim was marked failed. Expected now, with SIMPLE_NATIVE_GO_TO_END=1 and
# `native-build main.spl --backend=cranelift --entry-closure` from a copy of
# this directory outside test/ (closure builds exclude fixture trees): the
# build exits non-zero WITHOUT a signal, names yield_gen as the one failed
# module with the message above, and still compiles plain_good and main. If
# the per-file worker pool refuses for lack of memory, add
# SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP_WHOLE_PROGRAM=1.
use yield_gen.{yield_first}
use plain_good.{good_twice}

fn main():
    print "y={yield_first(1)} twice={good_twice(21)}"
